WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:01.720
- He's selling nuts too.

00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:04.061
He's selling nuts, this guy.

00:00:04.061 --> 00:00:06.301
I told him, this is my market.

00:00:06.301 --> 00:00:09.731
♪ I'm the Naked Cowboy ♪

00:00:09.731 --> 00:00:12.011
♪ Keep it revolving ♪

00:00:12.011 --> 00:00:15.450
(alarm clock beeping)
(slide guitar music)

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:18.400
I generally get up around
seven, when I sleep well.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:20.220
First thing I do, I walk
straight to the kitchen,

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:22.010
I put the coffee in the microwave.

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:23.410
I'm writing a journal every day,

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:25.790
and my journals, to me, are everything.

00:00:33.787 --> 00:00:35.030
You know, it's kind of
like you're just constantly

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:37.570
shooting for the stars,
looking at the big picture,

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:40.300
and you're basically, your life

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:41.860
follows the patter of your thoughts.

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:42.930
Life is tough.

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:44.930
It's hard to stay motivated, especially

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:46.670
if you're really keeping yourself moving.

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:48.053
People always say: do you work out?

00:00:48.053 --> 00:00:49.840
And I'm always like nope, it's a gift.

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:51.492
Pizza, beer, and cigarettes,

00:00:51.492 --> 00:00:52.580
that's all you need.

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:54.930
I'm driven to succeed, to get publicity,

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:56.500
to get numbers, to be seen,

00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:00.010
and to share, motivate,
inspire, influence,

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:01.849
and impact everyone.

00:01:01.849 --> 00:01:05.350
After about an hour,
sometimes two hours of that,

00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:09.600
I take a shower, basically
just get ready for work.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:10.433
(water splashing)
Most people don't know

00:01:10.433 --> 00:01:12.960
I have the fastest shave in the east.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:15.800
Well I have a huge underwear collection.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:17.900
My wife is constantly
putting 'em on boards,

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:19.560
painting 'em, and I'm constantly

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:21.210
getting a fresh supply of mediums.

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:23.450
When they're brand-new, it's
like putting on a new suit.

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:25.917
You're like, ah, I feel confident today!

00:01:25.917 --> 00:01:29.000
(light guitar music)

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.930
Towards the end of high
school, I would imagine,

00:01:38.930 --> 00:01:41.680
somebody told me about this
book, "Unlimited Power".

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:44.870
Up to that point, I was a crazy, wild kid,

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:46.200
in trouble all the time,

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:49.420
going to the courthouse for,
you name it, 50 different

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:51.290
juvenile misconduct stuff.

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:52.470
I'm reading the book and this guy says

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:54.240
I could be anything I
want, I could be rich,

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:55.548
successful and everything else.

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:57.810
Somebody actually, instead of
saying I can't do something,

00:01:57.810 --> 00:01:59.200
said I could do something.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:00.960
I was trying to be a country singer,

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:03.540
a model, an actor, or a body-builder.

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:06.080
When I went to Venice
Beach, California, 1998,

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:07.586
to shoot for Playgirl magazine,

00:02:07.586 --> 00:02:08.419
(whistling)
I went and played

00:02:08.419 --> 00:02:10.970
on the beach in a cowboy
outfit, with my clothes,

00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:12.650
was ignored the entire day.

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:14.970
The photographer who was shooting me naked

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:16.560
said why don't you play in your underwear.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:17.960
I knew when I got in my underwear

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:19.480
and did it, and nobody came over, I knew

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:20.360
it right then and there.

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:22.970
So that was, you know,
the birth of Naked Cowboy,

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:23.803
if you will.

00:02:23.803 --> 00:02:26.010
I went back to Cincinnati, my hometown,

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:27.770
did the same thing I did at Venice Beach,

00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:29.010
I got in my underwear and boots and hat

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:30.530
in the parking garage,
came out and played.

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:32.320
People went crazy, took pictures,

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:33.450
and then the police arrested me

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:36.610
and I got like a $69, or
something like that, citation.

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:38.704
But I got on the morning
show the next day.

00:02:38.704 --> 00:02:40.538
(laughing)
♪ Well I'm the Naked Cowboy ♪

00:02:40.538 --> 00:02:42.840
Sorry to interrupt you.
- Oh, we like it.

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:45.750
- So I paid $69 and I'm on TV,

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:47.650
and I'm talking about how I'm
gonna be the most celebrated

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:48.500
entertainer of all time,

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:50.210
I'm advertising Naked Cowboy.

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:52.080
I basically went from Cincinnati

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:53.510
all the way to Key West, Florida,

00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:54.770
and they got the news
almost in every city.

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:56.010
I call the police and the news.

00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:56.843
How could I not?

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:58.900
And then a friend suggested going east,

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:01.210
'cause he said I could get
arrested every two or three hours

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:03.370
instead of every 10 or 12 hours.

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:04.560
The cities are closer together.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:06.670
I went east for that reason.

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:08.130
Happened to go to New York,

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:10.070
happened to fall into Times Square,

00:03:10.070 --> 00:03:12.550
got a cheap hotel and came
back for the second day.

00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:14.400
Two days became 16 years.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.550
My goal was never to
be a street performer,

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:18.600
and get a dollar and
a dollar and a dollar.

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:20.500
Ultimately, that's what it's come to.

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:25.490
But the whole point was,
get very successful,

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:28.750
create a brand, and
sell products worldwide,

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:29.960
and get checks in the mail

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:33.090
for the rest of my life.
(light acoustic guitar music)

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:37.190
Almost 18 years, nearly every single day.

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:40.040
My routine of going in and everything,

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:42.550
I'd like to say it gets
easier all the time,

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:46.230
but the winter's a tough time
of year for a naked cowboy.

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:48.330
If it's 20 degrees, like it's been lately,

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:51.580
you're looking at 30 minutes,
two hours in a garage,

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:54.400
30 minutes, when I come
out of the cold especially,

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.244
your body's all tight and it's tense.

00:03:56.244 --> 00:03:59.060
Working out is a stress reliever,

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:00.482
and it just warms you up.

00:04:00.482 --> 00:04:04.315
